==English==

===Etymology===
{{unk|en}} etymology, 1813.<ref>{{R:Merriam Webster Online}}</ref> Original sense “alcoholic drink”, possibly a variant of {{m|en|switchel||a drink of molasses and water, often mixed with rum}}, attested 1790, itself of uncertain origin.<ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary}}</ref> Possibly influenced by {{m|en|swirl}} or {{m|en|fizz}}.

In verb sense “to stir”, from {{m|en|swizzle stick||stick for stirring alcoholic drinks}}, itself attested 1859.

